<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="channel_volunteers" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Volunteer Coordination</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html">
            <p>Setting up roles and shifts, running the day, screening
            volunteers, and reporting hours.</p>
        </field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('event.group_event_user')])]" />
    </record>

    <!-- ================= Section 1: Roles and shifts ================= -->
    <record id="section_roles" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Roles and shifts</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_roles_shifts" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Adding roles to an event, and running one as shifts</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>Open the event and go to its <strong>Volunteers</strong> tab.
            Add a role - a name ("Setup Crew", "Greeter", "Net Control"), how
            many people it needs, and a short description volunteers will
            see on the website.</p>
            <p>A role can be filled as one block for the whole event, or
            broken into timed shifts. To do the latter, tick <strong>Run as
            Shifts</strong> on the role, then add shifts - each is a time
            window and a slot count. The <strong>Shifts</strong> stat button
            on the event shows them on a calendar.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_recurring" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Recurring shifts for a weekly program</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>On an <strong>Event Type</strong> (Events ›
            Configuration › Event Types), add Recurring Volunteer
            Shift lines: role name, weekday, start time, length, slots. Give
            your recurring event that type, and a nightly job creates the
            matching shifts as far ahead as the horizon in settings -
            without duplicating ones it's already made. Need them sooner?
            Open the event and click <strong>Generate shifts from event
            type</strong>.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ===================== Section 2: On the day ===================== -->
    <record id="section_day" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">On the day</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_checkin" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Check-in, check-out, and no-shows</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>Front desk opens the shift and clicks <strong>Check In</strong>
            as each volunteer arrives, <strong>Check Out</strong> when they
            leave - hours are calculated automatically from the two
            timestamps. If someone didn't show up, click
            <strong>No-show</strong> on their assignment: it's kept for the
            record but left out of hours reports.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_swaps" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Shift swaps</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>A volunteer can offer a shift for swap from their own page.
            Another volunteer claims it. The coordinator approves it under
            <strong>Events › Shift Swaps</strong>, which reassigns
            the shift - the volunteer taking it still has to meet whatever
            screening the role requires.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================== Section 3: Screening =================== -->
    <record id="section_screening" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Screening volunteers</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">30</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_screening_records" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Skills, background checks &amp; waivers</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">31</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>All set up on the volunteer's own contact record, under the
            <strong>Volunteer</strong> tab. Tag <strong>Skills</strong>
            (First Aid, Spanish, Licensed Driver…) from the list under
            Events › Configuration › Volunteer Skills.</p>
            <p>For a <strong>background check</strong>: set it to Requested
            when you start one, and click <strong>Mark Cleared</strong> once
            it comes back - that stamps today's date and sets the re-check
            due date from the validity in settings. A nightly job flips
            lapsed checks to Expired and raises a to-do for the Volunteer
            Coordinator ahead of expiry, so nobody has to watch a
            calendar.</p>
            <p>For a <strong>liability waiver</strong>: print it from the
            contact's Print menu (it adapts for minors), collect the signed
            copy, then click <strong>Record Waiver Accepted</strong> to
            stamp the date. For a minor, tick <strong>Under 18</strong> and
            record the parent/guardian - the waiver PDF picks them up
            automatically.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_require_it" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Making a role require it</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">32</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>On the volunteer role, tick <strong>Requires Background
            Check</strong> and/or <strong>Requires Waiver</strong>, and add
            any <strong>Required Skills</strong>. From then on, a sign-up -
            on the website or in the back office - from a volunteer who
            isn't cleared, hasn't a current waiver, or lacks a skill is
            refused, with a message saying exactly what's missing.</p>
            <p>Looking for the right person instead? Click <strong>Suggest
            Volunteers</strong> on a shift to get everyone who has every
            required skill, is cleared and waivered as the role needs, and
            isn't already booked on an overlapping shift.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================== Section 4: Reporting ==================== -->
    <record id="section_reporting" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Reporting</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">40</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_hours" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Volunteer hours and certificates</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">41</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p><strong>Events › Volunteer Reporting ›
            Volunteer Hours</strong> is a pivot by volunteer, program,
            event, or month. <strong>Hours Certificates</strong> print a
            per-volunteer PDF for a chosen year, listing every shift and the
            total - handy for students and court-ordered service.
            <strong>Understaffed Shifts</strong> lists upcoming shifts still
            short of people.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ========================= Quiz ========================= -->
    <record id="slide_quiz" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Check your understanding</field>
        <field name="slide_category">quiz</field>
        <field name="sequence">90</field>
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q1" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="question">A role needs a background check. What happens if an uncleared volunteer tries to sign up?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">The sign-up is refused, with a message saying what's missing</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's allowed, with a warning email sent later</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's allowed only from the back office, not the website</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's allowed, since background checks are informational only</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q2" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="question">Who gets notified before a volunteer's background check expires?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">The Volunteer Coordinator, via an automatic to-do</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">Nobody - you have to check manually</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">The volunteer only, by text message</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">The front desk, at check-in</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q3" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="question">How do recurring weekly shifts get created?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">You add each one by hand every week</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">A nightly job builds them from Recurring Volunteer Shift lines on the event type</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Volunteers create their own shifts</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">They copy from last year's event automatically with no setup</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q4" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="question">A volunteer didn't show up for their shift. What do you click?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Delete their assignment</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">No-show</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Check In, then Check Out immediately</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Offer the shift for swap on their behalf</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

</odoo>
